    "narrative": "LawDog\u2019s strongest plays for this July 26 slate are headlined by **Dylan Beavers** (68.38) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (68.19), both of whom benefit from highly favorable matchups against back-end rotation arms. **Dylan Beavers** finds himself in an ideal environment; he is bolstered by a significant 16% park factor boost and a 10% edge against Lopez, while securing a leadoff spot that maximizes his impact on our scarcest category: stolen bases. Similarly, **Geraldo Perdomo** benefits from a strong 17% SP skill advantage against Mikolas. While **Bryce Harper** (67.44) and **Taylor Ward** (64.51) remain locked as high-floor, high-upside starters, the emphasis today is on leveraging lineup position and park factors to chase speed and counting stats.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved the outfield and utility spots, where **Daulton Varsho** (45.39) narrowly missed the cut. While **Daulton Varsho** benefits from a \"Slow SP Delivery\" factor\u2014a key metric we prioritize for his SB potential\u2014his efficiency score was ultimately suppressed by a difficult matchup against Suarez and unfavorable wind conditions. Consequently, the optimizer favored the higher raw efficiency of **JJ Bleday** and **Gavin Sheets**, despite their own platoon disadvantages. We must remain cautious with **Cal Raleigh** (44.02), who faces a legitimate challenge today against deGrom; his score is significantly dragged down by a -19% SP skill penalty. Although **Cal Raleigh** remains in the lineup due to positional scarcity, his output against such an elite arm carries inherent risk that could impact our collective AVG efficiency.",
